# Changelog (engine/v1/)

## Tube loops gated on the centerline direction
**What:** A loop on a tube now engages only when its axis lies within 45° of the tube's centerline tangent nearest the player. Non-tube loop surfaces engage on any axis, as before. Only engagement is gated; a running loop is not released on a mismatch.
- `buildTube` returns its centerline: node centers plus connector ring points.
- `computeWorldCenterline` stores it in world space as `mesh.centerline` on the invisible, void and normal `BuildObject` paths (`null` for non-tubes).
- `sceneGraph.tubeCenterlines` maps a surface id to its centerline lines, gathered from terrain, void terrain and obstacle parts.
- `alongTube` is the last engage condition in `trackLoop`.

**Where:** [builder/NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js) (`buildTube`, `computeWorldCenterline`, `BuildObject`), [builder/NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js) (`tubeCenterlines`), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js) (`alongTube`, `trackLoop`).

## Small-loop roll exception limited to tube walls
**What:** `frame.onSmallLoop` now also requires `alongTube` for the slope's tilt axis (`cross(world up, alignedUp)`). A tube's walls, which tilt around its centerline, still don't roll. A bend along the tube's length rolls like a regular slope. Non-tube small-loop surfaces are unchanged.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js) (`detectSituation`).

## Void wall linings wound to face the cavity
**What:** Void wall linings now face into the cavity. Each void face carries `flipWinding` (`cavitySign < 0`), and `buildHostLining` pushes that face's lining triples as (a, c, b) when it is set.

**Where:** [builder/NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js) (`buildVoidFaces`, `buildHostLining`).

## Backface culling skips water and planes
**What:** `setFaceCulling(gl, cull)` turns on `CULL_FACE` only when `cull` is true and `CONFIG.Performance.BackfaceCulling` is on. It replaces the frame-start toggle in `drawScene`. Culling is set per mesh in `drawMeshList`, and is off for `primitive === "plane"` and for `options.cull === false`. `drawWaterPass` passes `cull: false`. The scatter instance, scatter decal and mesh decal passes also skip planes. Scatter instance results now carry `primitive`.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`setFaceCulling`, `drawMeshList`, `drawWaterPass`, `drawDecalPass`, `drawScatterDecalPass`, `buildScatterInstanceBuffers`, `drawScene`).

## trackLoop reads contactGrace
**What:** `contactGrace` is added to the `playerState` destructure in `trackLoop`, which fixes a ReferenceError on the first airborne frame.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js) (`trackLoop`).

## Trigger overlay split at the water line
**What:** The main mesh program has a `v_worldY` varying and a `u_waterClip` uniform (x = water level in world units, y = side kept: +1 above, −1 below, 0 keeps all). Clipped fragments get alpha 0 and are discarded. `drawMeshList` sets `u_waterClip` on every non-triplanar call (default `keepWholeMesh`). `drawTriggerOverlay` replaces PASS C. With water, `drawTranslucentPass` draws the far-side trigger half before the water and the near-side half after it. Without water, triggers draw whole before the translucents.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`createProgram`, `drawMeshList`, `drawTriggerOverlay`, `drawTranslucentPass`, `drawScene`).

## Triggers unculled and anchored at their authored base
**What:** `drawTriggerOverlay` passes `cull: false`. `buildTriggerMesh` centres the box at `start.y + triggerHeight * 0.5`, so the drawn and detected box spans `start.y` to `world.height`.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`drawTriggerOverlay`), [builder/NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js) (`buildTriggerMesh`).

## Toon and comic filters
**What:** `CONFIG.Rendering.Filters` is `{ ToonLines, Comic }` (replaces `Outlines`); both currently `true`. New exported `FILTER_TUNING` outside `API_CONFIG`: `Lines { Color, Width, Threshold }` and `Comic { LightDirection, Bands, ShadowFloor, ColorLevels, Halftone { CellSize, Strength } }`.
- `comicLightGLSL` in `createFoggedTextureFragmentShader` multiplies every surface program's color by a light band. The band comes from the screen-space face normal (turned toward the camera) and `FILTER_TUNING.Comic.LightDirection`, and is gated by a new `u_comic` uniform set in `configureTexturedMeshPass` from `passState.comic`.
- When either filter is on, `drawScene` draws into `renderer.sceneTarget` (RGBA8 color + DEPTH_COMPONENT24 depth textures from `ensureSceneTarget`, resized with the canvas). `drawFilterPass` (PASS F, after the translucent pass, before the debug overlays) then draws it to the canvas through `createFilterProgram`:
  - posterize plus halftone dots on geometry, when Comic is on
  - ink lines where inverse view depth bends, faded by fog, when ToonLines is on
  - the scene depth is written through `gl_FragDepth` with `depthFunc(ALWAYS)`
- With both filters off, the scene draws straight to the canvas as before.

**Where:** [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`API_CONFIG.Rendering.Filters`, `FILTER_TUNING`), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`comicLightGLSL`, `createFoggedTextureFragmentShader`, `createFilterProgram`, `createTargetTexture`, `ensureSceneTarget`, `ensureFilterQuad`, `ensureLevelRenderer`, `configureTexturedMeshPass`, `drawFilterPass`, `drawScene`).

## Toon lines under scatter and water; softer comic
**What:**
- **Ink pass:** ToonLines moved to `drawInkPass` (PASS E2, after decals, before scatter). The pass blits scene depth into `sceneTarget.edgeDepth` through `edgeFramebuffer`, then alpha-blends ink from `createInkProgram` onto the scene color. It drops ink for pixels whose rebuilt world height is on the far side of the water from the camera (`u_waterClip`).
- **Filter pass:** `createFilterProgram` now does comic and presenting only, sharing `fullscreenVertexGLSL`. Comic skips the sky. Posterize blends by `Posterize.Strength`, and halftone dots form only below `Halftone.Below` brightness.
- **`FILTER_TUNING.Comic`:**
  - `ColorLevels` replaced by `Posterize { Levels, Strength }`
  - `Halftone` gains `Below`
  - `ShadowFloor` changes from 0.6 to 0.75

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`fullscreenVertexGLSL`, `createInkProgram`, `createFilterProgram`, `ensureInkQuad`, `ensureSceneTarget`, `ensureLevelRenderer`, `drawInkPass`, `drawFilterPass`, `drawScene`), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`FILTER_TUNING`).

## Antialiased filter target
**What:**
- **Multisampled target:** when filtered, `sceneTarget.framebuffer` draws into multisampled renderbuffers (`colorSamples` RGBA8, `depthSamples` DEPTH_COMPONENT24) at `FILTER_TUNING.Samples` (4) samples.
- **Resolves:** `resolveSceneTarget` blits the scene into `resolveFramebuffer`, which holds the `color`/`depth` textures, in `drawFilterPass` (color and depth). It blits into `edgeFramebuffer` in `drawInkPass` (depth).
- **Cleanup removed:** the texture unbinds after both passes are gone.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`ensureSceneTarget`, `resolveSceneTarget`, `drawInkPass`, `drawFilterPass`), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`FILTER_TUNING.Samples`).
